Heap: stores `new String("abc")`;
Stack: stores local variable `int x = 5;` in a method;
Metaspace: holds `java.lang.String` class metadata.

G1 divides heap into regions and prioritizes regions with most garbage;
ZGC uses colored pointers for concurrent marking;
Parallel GC uses multiple threads for Young generation collection.

Set heap: `-Xmx4g -Xms4g`;
Enable heap dump: `-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError`;
Use G1 GC: `-XX:+UseG1GC`.

